        "start": 0,
        "end": 790,
        "text": "I strongly doubt if we will ever understandand fully evaluate -the 60s without placing it against the background of another radical decade, the 30s. Having lived out both periods up to the hilt, I find that my older contemporaries as well as the younger people with whom I worked twenty years ago have seldom been able to distance themselves sufficiently from their time to draw these crucial comparisons adequately. Recent biographies by old New York socialists and communists who lived with such nostalgic exhilaration in the era climaxed by the Spanish Civil War and CIO organizing drives seem utterly estranged and uncomprehending in their attitudes toward the new left and counterculture. By the same token, the younger people of '68 and of New York's Lower Eastside and San Francis247",
